## Advanced Topics

### Memory Management

NLM uses modern C++ memory management practices:

```cpp
// Smart pointers for automatic memory management
auto config = std::make_shared<nlm::Config>();
auto brain = std::make_shared<nlm::Brain>(config);

// Move semantics for efficient transfers
auto newBrain = std::make_shared<nlm::Brain>(std::move(oldBrain));

// Pimpl idiom for implementation hiding
class Config {
private:
    struct Impl;
    std::unique_ptr<Impl> pImpl;
};
```

### Concurrency

Thread-safe operations where appropriate:

```cpp
// Global logger is thread-safe for read operations
nlm::Logger::getGlobal().info("Message from multiple threads");

// Configuration updates require external synchronization
config->set("parameter", value); // Thread-safe
config->loadFromFile("file");    // Thread-safe
```

### Performance Optimization

Performance considerations for high-performance applications:

```cpp
// Use const references for parameter passing
void processInput(const SensoryInput& input);

// Pre-allocate memory for performance
std::vector<Neuron> neurons;
neurons.reserve(config->getOr("neuron_count", 1000));

// Use move operations for temporary objects
auto temp = expensiveOperation();
brain->receiveSensoryInput(std::move(temp));
```

## Error Handling

### Common Error Conditions

- **Configuration errors**: Invalid or missing configuration values
- **Memory allocation failures**: Out of memory situations
- **File I/O errors**: Configuration file access issues
- **Initialization failures**: Brain setup problems
- **Runtime errors**: Invalid operations during simulation

### Error Code Enum

```cpp
enum class NLMErrorCode {
    Success = 0,
    ConfigFileNotFound = 1,
    InvalidConfigValue = 2,
    MemoryAllocationFailed = 3,
    BrainInitializationFailed = 4,
    InvalidOperation = 5,
    FileWriteFailed = 6,
    SimulationTimeout = 7
};
```

### Error Handling Pattern

```cpp
// Example error handling
auto result = brain->initialize();
if (!result) {
    auto error = nlm::Logger::getGlobal().getLastError();
    std::cerr << "Brain initialization failed: " << error.message << std::endl;
    return static_cast<int>(error.code);
}
```

